	<key>DESCRIPTION</key>
	<string>Knobs/Buttons 1,5,9,13 control layer alpha and select layer.  Knobs 2, 3, 4 control additive RGB.  When toggled with corresponding button, they control subtractive RGB.  Knobs6,7,8, control saturation, lightness, contrast, and their corresponding buttons toggle enabled state of those pixelFX. Knobs 10,11,12 control speed, scale, and transition time.  Buttons 13 and 14 control master inversion and flash.  Button 15 toggles the layer alpha and selection controls between Group A and Group B, and Knob 15 controls crossfader.  Option+\ turns on a second layer, which sends MIDI output to the port specified in the second port list.  This is for use with IAC bus, to map to another software (specifically intended for sending to Synesthesia.live).  The script has been rewroked with a rudimentary event distribution framework which appears to be working well and is easily reassignable for use in further programming or as a foundation for other scripting with different controllers.   b.92 (2026-10-24): in forward mode the knob rings also follow dots: CC 0-15 on channel 1 arriving from DotsOutput update knobs 1-16 (set feedbackSource in the init script for another app).  Also fixes the forwarded knob values being scaled by 127 twice when the LEDs refresh.  The original is still Twister.m8m; run one or the other, not both.  b.96: dots's section colours light the knobs in forward mode, and entering forward mode (or picking the forward port) asks dots for all its values, so the rings start right.  The forward port defaults to DotsInput when dots is running.  b.97: side button 12 (next to the forward-mode button) flips forward mode to dots's second page (CC 16-31: motionId and the effect sizes) and back.  b.98: in forward mode the bottom row of knob buttons (13-16) sends dots prev track, next track, prev scene, next scene.  b.99: the page toggle moves to knob button 16 (the side button only switches between Modul8 and dots); prev track, next track, prev scene, next scene move to knob buttons 9-12.  b.100: prev track, next track, prev scene, next scene move to the top row of knob buttons (1-4); dots's colours are re-applied whenever the lights are redrawn in forward mode.  b.101: Modul8 mode is fully switched off in dots mode: Modul8's events no longer reach the Twister, and the layer-select and RGB shift wiring is unhooked until Modul8 mode comes back.  b.104: in dots mode only the buttons with a dots function work (1-4 track and scene, 16 page); the rest are inert and keep their section colour.  Diagnostic logging removed (the log keeps just the load line and the first message from each MIDI source).</string>
